{"timestamp": "2026-09-13T20:07:02.210755+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3fcc348a-69dd-4967-9f68-b941e8f0e705', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You prepare the educational structure of one approved lesson.\\n\\nThe path owns the objective and concept identity. The skeleton owns section\\ncount, order, identity, visual requirement, and purpose.\\nA later planner will choose page blocks. You must not choose components, page\\nobjects, layouts, or question text.\\n\\n## FIXED INPUT\\n\\n- objective and objective_hash\\n- concept_id\\n- primary_knowledge_type\\n- lesson_mode\\n- ordered skeleton slots\\n- scope_contract\\n- prior_established\\n- explicit prerequisites\\n- lesson_actuals\\n- carried anchor, when present\\n- resource identity and purpose\\n\\n## YOUR DECISIONS\\n\\n1. Draft zero to three real misconceptions. Each must support a confident wrong\\n   answer. A missing term is a knowledge gap, not a misconception.\\n2. Reuse the carried anchor when it fits. Otherwise choose one concrete anchor\\n   and state why it is new.\\n3. Give each fixed section a concise title and transition note. Return exactly\\n   one section payload per supplied slot, in the supplied order.\\n   The first section\\'s transition_note must be null; only later sections\\n   may explain how they follow the preceding section.\\n4. Do not output technical identity. The backend attaches objective, concept id,\\n   section id/role, card_id, and visual_required after your response.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n- Never output or rewrite the objective or concept ID.\\n- Never add, remove, reorder, or rename a skeleton slot.\\n- Never choose a component, page object, pedagogical block intent, placement,\\n  or visual form.\\n- Never write question text.\\n- Never reteach prior_established in the structural rationale.\\n- Never introduce must_not_introduce content.\\n- Never manufacture a misconception to fill a count.\\n- Never choose page blocks, intents, objects, or briefs. A later planner\\n  owns the teaching design.\\n\\nIf the objective cannot honestly fit the skeleton, emit deviation_request.\\nIf the objective itself is wrong, emit objective_concern. Do not repair either.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only, matching the supplied output schema.\\n\\nThe output contains only:\\n\\n- anchor as {\"description\": str, \"source\": \"carried\"|\"new\"}\\n- one semantic concept-card payload (title/prereqs/misconceptions/opens_by;\\n  no id or objective)\\n- sections with title and transition_note only, one per supplied slot in order\\n- deviation_request or null\\n- objective_concern or null\\n\\nIt contains no components and no blocks.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n1. Did I avoid outputting upstream-owned identity/objective fields?\\n2. Did I return exactly one section payload per fixed slot, in order?\\n3. Does every misconception pass the confident-wrong-answer test?\\n4. Did I choose any page form or teaching block? Remove it.\\n5. Did I contradict prior_established, terminology, or exclusions?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"PathAnchor\": {\"properties\": {\"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source\": {\"enum\": [\"carried\", \"new\"], \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"description\", \"source\"], \"title\": \"PathAnchor\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathDeviationRequest\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"operation\": {\"enum\": [\"insert\", \"remove\", \"replace\", \"reorder\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"target_slot\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"replacement_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"operation\", \"target_slot\", \"replacement_slot\", \"reason\"], \"title\": \"PathDeviationRequest\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralMisconception\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"description\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"The wrong belief, stated the way a learner would state it.\"}, \"statement\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"source\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralMisconception\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralPageCard\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"title\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"prereqs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"misconceptions\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralMisconception\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"no_known_misconceptions\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"opens_by\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralPageCard\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralPageSection\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"title\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"transition_note\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"title\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralPageSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"anchor\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathAnchor\"}, \"cards\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralPageCard\"}, \"maxItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralPageSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"deviation_request\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathDeviationRequest\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"objective_concern\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"anchor\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralPagePlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"concept_id\": \"fce6a245-18bb-4cdf-9fc9-0d81a6f2ebb0\",\\n  \"exclusions\": [],\\n  \"external_prerequisites\": [],\\n  \"group_ids\": [],\\n  \"groups\": [],\\n  \"lesson_actuals\": [],\\n  \"must_establish\": [\\n    \"Plants are living things that can produce their own food\",\\n    \"Plants are called producers\",\\n    \"Use one concrete classroom example.\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_whole_lesson\": true,\\n  \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n  \"objective_hash\": \"d6f7d6cad2c469360860d8f8ebf12437b752a3a886ff4f730711219ad36db08c\",\\n  \"prerequisites\": [],\\n  \"primary_knowledge_type\": \"conceptual\",\\n  \"prior_established\": [\\n    \"plants have roots, stems and leaves\",\\n    \"living things need food to grow\"\\n  ],\\n  \"scope_contract\": {\\n    \"assumed_prerequisites\": [],\\n    \"may_include\": [],\\n    \"must_establish\": [\\n      \"Explain that plants make their own food (are producers)\",\\n      \"Identify leaves as the site of photosynthesis and chlorophyll as the light-capturing substance\",\\n      \"Describe photosynthesis as using light, carbon dioxide, and water to produce food and oxygen\",\\n      \"Explain why light is essential for photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"chloroplast organelles\",\\n      \"chemical equations of photosynthesis (e.g., 6CO\\\\u2082 + 6H\\\\u2082O \\\\u2192 C\\\\u2086H\\\\u2081\\\\u2082O\\\\u2086 + 6O\\\\u2082)\",\\n      \"glucose as a specific sugar\",\\n      \"light-dependent and light-independent reactions\",\\n      \"limiting factors of photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"notation\": null,\\n    \"terminology\": []\\n  },\\n  \"secondary_demand\": null,\\n  \"shared_preparation\": true,\\n  \"slots\": [\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"instance_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"locked\": true,\\n      \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n      \"role\": \"check\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"title\": \"Plants as Producers\",\\n  \"variant_previews\": [\\n    {\\n      \"group_profile\": \"core\",\\n      \"slots\": [\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n          \"role\": \"orient\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Build the idea itself. State it, ground it, make it usable.\",\\n          \"role\": \"explain\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": false,\\n          \"purpose\": \"Put a case and a near-miss side by side. The learner must see the boundary of the idea, not just the idea.\\\\n\",\\n          \"role\": \"contrast\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"locked\": true,\\n          \"purpose\": \"The shared diagnostic. Identical across every variant. Written from the card only, never from the prose above it.\\\\n\",\\n          \"role\": \"check\",\\n          \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n          \"visual_required\": false\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"toggles_applied\": [\\n        \"misconception.confront_per_belief\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 16000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
