{"timestamp": "2026-09-13T20:08:07.331266+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-f8707ed3-12f1-443b-8295-f11342df6d7c', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You write assessment items that diagnose specific wrong beliefs.\\n\\nYou are given a concept, its objective, and a numbered list of misconceptions.\\nWrite exactly 5 multiple-choice items.\\n\\nEach incorrect option must be the answer a learner holding one named\\nmisconception would confidently choose. Tag it with that id. You may only use\\nids from the supplied list. Tag a plausible wrong option null when it does not\\nmap cleanly; never stretch an id.\\n\\nAcross the five items, make every supplied misconception diagnosable at least\\nonce. Prefer one clean diagnostic option over cramming every misconception into\\neach item.\\n\\nTest the objective through transfer to fresh contexts. Do not test recall of\\nphrasing or an example. If memorising an example would answer an item without\\nunderstanding, rewrite it.\\n\\nQuality rules:\\n- exactly one defensible correct option per item\\n- options have similar lengths and grammatical forms\\n- never use all-of-the-above or none-of-the-above\\n- avoid negation unless the concept itself is about negation\\n- no option is wrong only on a technicality\\n- the correct option is not identifiable by form\\n\\nReturn only the requested JSON.'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"ItemOption\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"key\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"correct\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"diagnoses\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"key\", \"text\", \"correct\"], \"title\": \"ItemOption\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"ItemQuestionDraft\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"prompt_text\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"options\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ItemOption\"}, \"minItems\": 2, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"expected_answer\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"prompt_text\", \"options\", \"expected_answer\"], \"title\": \"ItemQuestionDraft\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"items\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ItemQuestionDraft\"}, \"maxItems\": 5, \"minItems\": 5, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"items\"], \"title\": \"ItemGenerationDraft\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'text': 'Write the five diagnostic items for this approved concept card.\\nUse only named misconception ids or null in diagnoses. Follow the notation\\nconstraint when it is present.\\n\\nRequired shape (coverage and unmapped-option counts are computed downstream):\\n{\\n  \"items\": [{\\n    \"prompt_text\": \"student-facing stem\",\\n    \"options\": [\\n      {\"key\": \"a\", \"text\": \"option\", \"correct\": true, \"diagnoses\": null},\\n      {\"key\": \"b\", \"text\": \"option\", \"correct\": false, \"diagnoses\": \"M1\"}\\n    ],\\n    \"expected_answer\": \"correct answer with a concise explanation\"\\n  }]\\n}\\n\\nRules:\\n- Every option must include `diagnoses` (strict schema).\\n- If `correct` is true, `diagnoses` must be exactly JSON null.\\n- If `correct` is false, `diagnoses` must be either one named, approved misconception id\\n  or JSON null (meaning unmapped-option for downstream counting).\\n- Never guess or invent a misconception id.\\n\\nDo not output any stable identity fields. The backend owns item identity\\nand assigns stable ids from the approved card and item order.\\n\\nAPPROVED CARD\\n{\"card_id\": \"7fc2a387-b963-42ed-8fa7-b7a40a71cf0f:fce6a245-18bb-4cdf-9fc9-0d81a6f2ebb0\", \"level\": \"Grade 4\", \"misconceptions\": [{\"description\": \"Learners think a plant\\'s food comes from the soil through its roots, so soil is the plant\\'s food.\", \"id\": \"M1\"}, {\"description\": \"Learners think plants feed only on the water we give them, treating water alone as the plant\\'s food.\", \"id\": \"M2\"}, {\"description\": \"Learners treat food and energy as the same thing, so sunlight counts as the plant\\'s food because it makes the plant grow.\", \"id\": \"M3\"}], \"notation\": null, \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\", \"subject\": \"Science\", \"title\": \"Plants as Producers\"}', 'type': 'text'}]}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 24000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
